# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and this package divide the work rather than overlap, along a single line:\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) und dieses Paket teilen die Arbeit auf, statt sich zu überschneiden, entlang einer einzigen Linie:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| ffsim owns                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | `qiskit-fermions` owns                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| The high-level ansatz *operators* ([`UCJOpSpinBalanced`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced \"(in ffsim)\"), [`UCCSDOpRestrictedReal`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal.html#ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal \"(in ffsim)\") and their siblings), built from coupled-cluster amplitudes or a parameter vector | The fermionic *circuit* ([`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")) those operators become, and its transpilation into a qubit circuit under any fermion-to-qubit encoding |\n"
"| Fast simulation in a compact fixed-particle-number space                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | The mapper framework and the operator data structures the circuit is built from                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
msgstr ""
"| ffsim ist zuständig für | `qiskit-fermions` ist zuständig für |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| Die übergeordneten Ansatz-*Operatoren* ([`UCJOpSpinBalanced`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced \"(in ffsim)\"), [`UCCSDOpRestrictedReal`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal.html#ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal \"(in ffsim)\") und ihre Verwandten), erstellt aus Coupled-Cluster-Amplituden oder einem Parametervektor | Den fermionischen *Circuit* ([`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")), zu dem diese Operatoren werden, und seine Transpilation in einen Qubit-Circuit unter einer beliebigen Fermion-zu-Qubit-Kodierung |\n"
"| Schnelle Simulation in einem kompakten Raum fester Teilchenzahl | Das Mapper-Framework und die Operator-Datenstrukturen, aus denen der Circuit erstellt wird |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The practical consequence runs both ways. The ansatz math lives in ffsim, so [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") and [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") take an ffsim operator directly as their input. Conversely, ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, so lowering one of its ansatz operators through a *different* encoding is what bringing it here buys you.\n"
msgstr "Die praktische Folge gilt in beide Richtungen. Die Ansatz-Mathematik liegt in ffsim, sodass [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") und [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") einen ffsim-Operator direkt als Eingabe nehmen. Umgekehrt sind die eigenen Qiskit-Gates von ffsim spezifisch für die Jordan-Wigner-Transformation, sodass der Gewinn, einen seiner Ansatz-Operatoren hierher zu bringen, darin besteht, ihn über eine *andere* Kodierung abzusenken.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulation is where the two meet, and this guide explains how. ffsim is this package’s simulation backend, reached through its own protocols rather than a wrapper: the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) calls [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\"), [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\"), and [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") directly on [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")objects and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")objects, with no conversion step.\n"
msgstr "Die Simulation ist der Punkt, an dem sich beide treffen, und dieser Leitfaden erklärt, wie. ffsim ist das Simulations-Backend dieses Pakets, erreicht über seine eigenen Protokolle statt über einen Wrapper: Der [SKQD-Leitfaden](skqd#skqd-getting-started) ruft [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\"), [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") und [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") direkt auf [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")-Objekten und [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")-Objekten ohne Konvertierungsschritt auf.\n"

